WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.790
LILIANA YU: Google
Cloud Shell provides you

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.230
with command line access
to your cloud resources

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.910
directly from your browser.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.520
You can easily manage your
projects and resources

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.390
without having to install the
Google Cloud SDK or other tools

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:18.740
on your system.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.430
With Cloud Shell, the Cloud
SDK gcloud command line tool

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:26.240
and other utilities, we are
always available, up-to-date,

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.210
and fully authenticated
when you need them.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.310
Cloud Shell provides
command line access

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.160
to a virtual machine
instance in a terminal window

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.830
that opens in the web console.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.540
In this hands-on
lab, you will learn

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.640
how to connect to
computer resources

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.790
posted on Google Cloud
Platform via the web.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:47.450
You will learn how to use
Cloud Shell and gcloud command.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.850
We encourage students to
type the commands themselves,

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.490
to help encourage learning
at the core concepts.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:54.260
Many labs will include
a code block that

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.090
contains the required commands.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.040
You can easily copy
and paste the commands

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.290
from the code block into
the appropriate places

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:01.532
during the lab.

00:01:01.532 --> 00:01:02.990
When you're done
with this lab, you

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:07.250
will know how to launch Cloud
Shell and run gcloud commands.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.810
All you need to
work on this lab is

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:11.330
familiarity with standard
Linux text editors,

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:14.110
such as Vim, eMax, or Nano.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:16.730
And account, project,
and associated resources

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:19.340
are provided to
you on Quick Labs.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.670
This self-paced lab is part
of the Quick Labs quest GCP

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:23.810
essentials.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.060
Completing this quest
earns you this badge

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.100
to recognize your achievement.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.250
Next, you will provision
services with Cloud Launcher.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

